comment.body:
@ghajini, would you or anyone else perhaps be willing to help me with this?
https://github.com/AdguardTeam/AdguardFilters/issues/246295#issuecomment-7057929342

Of course, no worries at all if you'd rather not. I blacked out unrelated parts, if you're wondering. Thanks.

@AdamWr I isolated the trigger in Safari on my iPhone to **Fanboy’s Annoyances** in AdGuard for iOS. The installed list is version **2.1.68.88**, updated November 21, 2026.

With the list enabled, `www.theverge.com` shows the full-screen “Please allow ads on this site” warning. With the list disabled, the homepage loads normally. I re-enabled every other filter across all categories and confirmed the site still loads. AdGuard DNS Protection and uBlock Origin Lite stayed enabled during the comparison.

Could you check which rule in this list triggers the warning and whether it should be corrected in AdGuard or reported upstream to EasyList?
